From 88c60b71409a7b99e9cfec3c557143eae0dfbc5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 08:47:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 286: the relational mind does what a counter cannot - and the
 honesty gate was diluted

--mind relational --lie-dup 3. 4,417 parameters, no text and no absolute
coordinate reaching the weights. EVIDENCE_PARTIAL, and the three falsifiers
staked before the run split cleanly instead of blurring.

Passed: the train-control AUC FELL, 0.997 -> 0.841. Ranks re-shuffle on a
fresh tape, so the graph cannot be keyed the way a text can, and the number
says the class did the one thing it existed to do. Passed: matched coverage
reached nohid exactly - 0.431 against votes' 0.431, 1.000 against return's
0.889 - confirming the nine counters are derivable from the graph rather than
lost by leaving them out.

Passed, and this is the result the stage was for. On the duplicated lying
tape, the forged mention repeated three times, votes scores accuracy 0.000
across 40 answered items, reward -0.398. Not "worse than usual": exactly
zero, by construction, because a counter cannot distinguish three copies of
one witness from three witnesses. The relational mind scores 0.773 across 22
answered, reward 0.676, and 0.450 against votes' 0.000 at votes' own
coverage. That is not a better heuristic - it is a capability the counting
family does not possess. And the mechanism is visible rather than inferred:
duplicates arrive as pairs whose context-cosine rank and shared-rare-word
rank both sit at the top, and the model answers 0.36 of duplicated-lie sets
against 0.04 of ordinary contested ones. It acts precisely where the graph
says "one witness, repeated".

Failed: G_weighs_contested, on two contested answers held out at accuracy
0.0. Before calling that a defect - on that subset votes scores 0.121 against
a random-pick floor of 0.268, so majority reasoning is worse than chance
there and silence is the calibrated response. But two items is not evidence
of weighing either, and the gate is right to refuse.

The run also caught the honesty examiner measuring through a confound of its
own making. P(UNKNOWN) shares one softmax with however many candidate rows an
example happens to have, so it is mechanically diluted by |cands| - and
absent targets live in contested evidence, which has MORE candidates. The
measure was biased against the very hypothesis it tests. This arm made it
undeniable: at the argmax UNKNOWN won 0.714 of absent against 0.589 of
present, the correct ordering, while the mean probabilities were 0.478 and
0.484 and the AUC read 0.482 - chance. The logit margin over the best
candidate is what an argmax actually compares and it is invariant to how many
other rows exist, so the gate reads unknown_margin_auc now, with the
probability form kept beside it so earlier runs stay comparable.

Next: rerun this arm under the margin gate, minutes not hours, and then a
--lie-dup ladder at 1/2/3/5. Duplication is the one axis on which this mind
provably leaves the counting family, so it deserves a curve and not a point.

